From 791c01aa4dc12b9e0e36ad8e2817249591f04d72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:52:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DMP11/DMR11/DMC11: switch packs and boot on one board model
 with the DMV11

- One description per board (DMX_BOARD: pack names, switch positions and
  senses, MOP device type, boot ROM offset unit, SHOW SWITCHES texts)
  drives every SET/SHOW switch command, SHOW SWITCHES and the boot, for
  the DMV11, DMP11, DMR11 and DMC11.
- DMP11 (Unibus PDP-11): switch packs E121/E134 (MODE, TRIBUTARY,
  BOOTUNIT 0-15, {NO}POWERONBOOT, {NO}REMOTELOAD, PROGRAM, SWITCHES),
  power-on boot (BOOT DMPn), remote load detect and invoke primary MOP
  with MOP device type 18; the switch-assigned mode and tributary
  address also apply to the host interface.  Defaults: boot features off.
- DMR11 (DMC line with TYPE=DMR): switch packs E121/E134 (BOOTOFFSET,
  PASSWORD, PROGRAM, SWITCHES).  DMC11 (TYPE=DMC): line unit switch
  packs no. 2 (register 15, password) and no. 3 (register 16, boot ROM
  word offset), 377 as shipped.  Remote load detect (four equal password
  bytes) writes 173000+offset into 24, 0 into 26 and restarts the CPU
  through the power-fail trap when a boot ROM answers there (DEC's M9312
  DECnet ROM works); otherwise the board does the MOP load itself (DMR11
  device type 40, DMC11 Request Program 8,12,1).
- Remote load detect also sees an Enter MOP Mode that arrives while the
  host takes the line's messages.
- A reset keeps a scheduled connection poll (a program that executes
  RESET often, such as the M9312 DECnet ROM, starved it).
- Known issue 90: the shared DMP/DMV units are named after the device in
  use (SHOW DMV0 said DMP0); the DMP/DMV description names the device.
- Help texts for the DMP11, DMR11 and DMC11 switches and boot; HELP BOOT
  and HELP ROM (image format, BOOT CPU).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SuavtcpUxEC2vXhit3JaAg
